<title>COLOMBIA: Colombia's Simesa 1996 net profit rises.</title>
<headline>Colombia's Simesa 1996 net profit rises.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Siderugica de Medellin SA (Simesa), Colombia's third largest steel manufacturer, said its net profit rose to 2.51 billion pesos in 1996 from 2.09 billion in 1995.</p>
<p>A company statement reporting the earnings said it had notified Colombia's Securities Superintendency that it plans to pay out 1.76 billion of the '96 profit in dividends and leave the rest, about 30 percent, in reserve for future investment projects.</p>
<p>The dividend would amount to 24 pesos per share, it said.</p>
<p>((-- Javier Mozzo, Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944))</p>
